WEBVTT

00:09:59.153 --> 00:10:02.287
And this kind of habitat just goes
on and on and on for miles.

00:10:02.311 --> 00:10:04.245
This is Papua, New Guinea.

00:10:04.269 --> 00:10:08.804
Now little fishes and invertebrates
aren't the only things we see down there.

00:10:08.828 --> 00:10:10.102
We also see sharks,

00:10:10.126 --> 00:10:12.507
much more regularly
than I would have expected to.

00:10:12.531 --> 00:10:13.732
We're not quite sure why.

00:10:13.756 --> 00:10:16.865
What I want you to do now
is imagine yourself 400 feet underwater,

00:10:16.889 --> 00:10:18.897
with all this high-tech gear on your back,

00:10:18.921 --> 00:10:21.069
you're in a remote reef
off Papua, New Guinea,

00:10:21.093 --> 00:10:23.854
thousands of miles from the nearest
recompression chamber,

00:10:23.878 --> 00:10:26.289
and you're completely
surrounded by sharks.

00:10:26.313 --> 00:10:28.798
(Video) Diver 1: (In squeaky voice)
Look at those ...

00:10:28.822 --> 00:10:29.985
Diver 2: Uh, oh ...